ise rather than postprandially contradict the typical presentation of acute pancreatitis (B4) in favor of other visceral causes?", "summary": "Exercise-induced pain is atypical for pancreatitis (B4), slightly reducing its likelihood compared to other visceral causes."}], "differential_history": [], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "The patient exhibits signs of major haemodynamic instability (hypotension 80/40 mmHg, tachycardia 110/minute) requiring immediate intervention. Severe hypotension with compensatory tachycardia suggests shock, which could be related to an acute abdomen with potential internal bleeding (e.g., ruptured ectopic pregnancy, haemorrhagic pancreatitis, or other life-threatening causes).", "required_actions": ["Administer IV fluids (already initiated, but require escalation if unresponsive)", "Monitor for signs of end-organ perfusion (urine output, mental status, skin perfusion)", "Prepare for rapid diagnostic imaging (e.g., ultrasound for ectopic pregnancy, CT for pancreatitis/obstruction)"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": ""}, "turn_budget_used": 0, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.7, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.0, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Chronic pancreatitis'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": []